Brenda invested $300 into a scheme that accumulates simple interest at three-quarters of the original amount per year. How much in total will she have after 3 years?,Brenda invested $300 into a scheme that accumulates simple interest at the rate of three-quarters of the original amount per year. How much in total will she have after 3 years?,975,975,975,975,"Step 1: Identify principal (P), simple interest rate (r), and time (t).
- Principal P = $300
- Rate r = three-quarters of the original amount per year for simple interest. This means interest each year equals (3/4) of the principal: (3/4) × 300 = $225 per year.
- Time t = 3 years

Step 2: Compute total simple interest over 3 years.
- Total interest = yearly interest × years = 225 × 3 = $675

Step 3: Compute total amount after 3 years.
- Total amount = principal + total interest = 300 + 675 = $975

