"Carlos is planting a lemon tree. The tree costs $90 to plant. Each year it grows 7 lemons, selling for $1.5 each. It costs $3 a year to water and feed the tree. How many years will it take before he starts earning money on the lemon tree?","Carlos is planting a lemon tree. The tree will cost $90 to plant. Each year it will grow 7 lemons, which he can sell for $1.5 each. It costs $3 a year to water and feed the tree. How many years will it take before he starts earning money on the lemon tree?",13,13,12,13,"Let’s define variables:
- Initial planting cost: $90 (one-time)
- Each year:
  - Revenue: 7 lemons × $1.5 = $10.5
  - Cost: $3
  - Net profit per year: $10.5 − $3 = $7.5

We want the number of years n such that cumulative profit ≥ initial cost:
7.5n ≥ 90
n ≥ 90 / 7.5 = 12

So after 12 years, he starts earning money.

