"Aaron and Vanessa were relay race partners on a running team. Aaron was able to run each mile twice as fast as Vanessa, but Vanessa was able to run twice as far as Aaron did. If Vanessa ran 4 miles and Aaron completed his part of the race in 16 minutes, how long in minutes did Vanessa take to complete her part? It was a sunny day, perfect for a race.","Aaron and Vanessa were relay race partners on a running team. Aaron was able to run each mile twice as fast as Vanessa, but Vanessa was able to run twice as far as Aaron did. If Vanessa ran 4 miles and Aaron completed his part of the race in 16 minutes, how long in minutes did Vanessa take to complete her part?",64,64,64,64,"Let Aaron’s speed be v_A miles per minute and Vanessa’s speed be v_V miles per minute.
- Given: Aaron runs each mile twice as fast as Vanessa ⇒ v_A = 2 v_V.

Distances:
- Vanessa ran 4 miles.
- Vanessa runs twice as far as Aaron ⇒ Aaron ran 2 miles.

Aaron’s time:
- Given: Aaron completed his 2-mile part in 16 minutes.
- Time = distance / speed ⇒ 16 = 2 / v_A ⇒ v_A = 2/16 = 1/8 miles per minute.

Find Vanessa’s speed:
- v_V = v_A / 2 = (1/8)/2 = 1/16 miles per minute.

Vanessa’s time:
- Time = distance / speed = 4 / (1/16) = 64 minutes.

#### 64",,"Let Aaron’s speed be v_A miles per minute and Vanessa’s speed be v_V miles per minute.
- Given: Aaron runs each mile twice as fast as Vanessa ⇒ v_A = 2 v_V.
Distances:
- Vanessa ran 4 miles.
- Vanessa runs twice as far as Aaron ⇒ Aaron ran 2 miles.
Aaron’s time:
- Given: Aaron completed his 2-mile part in 16 minutes.
- Time = distance / speed ⇒ 16 = 2 / v_A ⇒ v_A = 2/16 = 1/8 miles per minute.
Find Vanessa’s speed:
- v_V = v_A / 2 = (1/8)/2 = 1/16 miles per minute.
Vanessa’s time:
- Time = distance / speed = 4 / (1/16) = 64 minutes.
#### 64","Let V be Vanessa’s speed (miles per minute). Then Aaron’s speed is 2V (since he runs each mile twice as fast).

Vanessa ran 4 miles. Aaron ran half as far as Vanessa (since Vanessa ran twice as far as Aaron), so Aaron ran 2 miles.

Aaron’s time = distance/speed = 2 miles / (2V) = 1/V minutes. We are told this equals 16 minutes, so:
1/V = 16 ⇒ V = 1/16 miles per minute.

Vanessa’s time = distance/speed = 4 miles / (1/16) = 64 minutes.

#### 64",,"Let V be Vanessa’s speed (miles per minute). Then Aaron’s speed is 2V (since he runs each mile twice as fast).
Vanessa ran 4 miles. Aaron ran half as far as Vanessa (since Vanessa ran twice as far as Aaron), so Aaron ran 2 miles.
Aaron’s time = distance/speed = 2 miles / (2V) = 1/V minutes. We are told this equals 16 minutes, so:
1/V = 16 ⇒ V = 1/16 miles per minute.
Vanessa’s time = distance/speed = 4 miles / (1/16) = 64 minutes.
