"There are 6 trees in Chris's yard, which he planted last year. Ferdinand has half the number of trees that Chris has. Harry has 5 more than twice the number of trees that Ferdinand has. How many more trees are in Harry's yard than Ferdinand's yard?",There are 6 trees in Chris's yard. Ferdinand has half the number of trees that Chris has. Harry has 5 more than twice the number of trees that Ferdinand has. How many more trees are in Harry's yard than Ferdinand's yard?,8,8,8,8,"Let's define the number of trees each person has:

